## 📖 About

**SkillPath** is a web app that helps you plan, track, and grow your programming skills. Pick what you want to learn, see the whole route laid out as a path, and schedule your study time on a calendar.

It covers:

- **Software engineering** — algorithms, data structures, system design, databases, testing, DevOps, version control, architecture, and more
- **Programming languages** — Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, Java, C/C++, C#, Go, Rust, PHP, Swift, Kotlin, SQL, and others
- **Web & app development** — frontend, backend, full-stack, mobile

---

## ✨ Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 🧭 **Path View** | Visual roadmap showing skills, prerequisites, and the order to learn them |
| 📅 **Calendar View** | Schedule lessons, practice sessions, and deadlines; see your week or month at a glance |
| 📚 **Skill Library** | Browse skills by category (engineering topics or languages) |
| ✅ **Progress Tracking** | Mark skills as *Not started / In progress / Completed* |
| 🎯 **Goals** | Set a target (e.g. "Become a backend developer") and get a suggested path |
| 🔍 **Search & Filter** | Find skills by language, level, or topic |
| 🌗 **Light / Dark Mode** | Comfortable on any screen |

---

## 🗺️ How the Path View Works

Each skill is a **node**. Lines between nodes show **prerequisites**.

```
Programming Basics ──► Data Structures ──► Algorithms ──► System Design
        │                                        │
        └──► Git & Version Control               └──► Competitive Programming
```

- **Gray** = locked (prerequisite not done)
- **Blue** = available
- **Yellow** = in progress
- **Green** = completed

Click any node to see resources, estimated time, and to add it to your calendar.

---

## 📅 Calendar View

- Day / Week / Month layouts
- Drag and drop to reschedule study sessions
- Link events to skills on your path
- Optional reminders and recurring sessions (e.g. "Python practice — every Mon & Wed")

